WEBVTT

00:13:58.250 --> 00:14:01.096
Eventually, I had to start
managing expectations.

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:03.696
Now my calendar invite
automatically notifies people

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:06.646
that I'm usually running
five to 10 minutes late.

00:14:06.670 --> 00:14:08.776
It helps them understand my schedule.

00:14:08.800 --> 00:14:10.800
But there's something
that helps even more.

00:14:10.824 --> 00:14:12.162
(Music)

00:14:12.206 --> 00:14:15.040
Alex Cornell: (Sings) Well, I've
been sittin' here all day /

00:14:15.064 --> 00:14:18.646
I've been sittin' in this waiting room.

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:22.009
AG: Hold music.
But not just any hold music.

00:14:22.033 --> 00:14:23.697
AC: (Sings) Waitin' on my friends /

00:14:23.697 --> 00:14:28.209
Yes, I'm waitin' on this conference call /

00:14:28.233 --> 00:14:29.466
All alone.

00:14:29.490 --> 00:14:31.281
AG: Now when I jump on the line late,